(36, 'World Photography Day - Ft. Homai Vyarawalla', 1, 'n', NULL, '<p><strong>INTRODUCTION</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Homai Vyarawalla (1913-2012), Modern India’s first female photojournalist, was a trailblazer in many regards. While defying traditional gender stereotypes, she also displayed exemplary journalistic courage while chronicling India’s euphoric yet painful transition towards becoming an independent nation-state. Her images retold the Partition from the eyes of the displaced and the decision-makers, along with a behind-the-scenes glimpse into a time that redefined the entire subcontinent.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>EARLY LIFE AND WORK</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ms. Vyarawalla was born in 1913 in India, where the quest for Independence was slowly picking up steam, but societal expectations of women were still somewhat archaic. Raised in a Parsi family, she was the lone female enrollee at the Sir Jamsetjee Jeejebhoy School of Art. Here, she fell in love with her craft and met her future husband and fellow journalist, Manekshaw Vyarawalla. From freelance assignments of group outings, Ms. Homai used the prima facie disapproval of others to gain experience and access to a plethora of significant events.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Her most memorable images humanized our freedom fighters, as epoch-defining decisions made the country experience great happiness alongside permanent scars. From an in-depth look at World War 2, stills from the Quit India Movement, the formation of the Constituent Assembly to the birth of India and Pakistan, Ms. Homai perfectly chronicled the birth of our Motherland. She also caught breathtakingly realistic images of a nation grieving the loss of life, communal divides, and the deep need of an entire civilization to re-announce itself to the planet after centuries of servitude.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>RECOGNITION AND LAURELS</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Employed at the prestigious British Information Services in the 1940s, her lifetime of work earned India’s second-highest civilian award, the Padma Vibhushan, in 2011. Her 104th birth anniversary was celebrated with a Google Doodle, where the moniker India’s “First Lady of the Lens” was aptly attached to the photojournalist. Her knack for capturing crucial moments of India’s struggle for Independence and her irreverence for gender norms make her among India’s finest photographers to date.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCSI4tz_l0aAjn7_8U35n7kQ\">Learn Photography by Balan Madhavan, Senior Fellow of the International League of Conservation Photographers</a></p>', NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, '', NULL, 'world-photography-day-ft-homai-vyarawalla.jpg', NULL, 'World Photography Day - Ft. Homai Vyarawalla', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, '2021-08-18 08:03:34', 4, '27.62.5.84', '2021-09-15 05:18:25', 4, '106.197.20.254', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'photography-day-ft-homai-vyarawalla', 'This World Photography Day, NatyaSutraOnline honors India’s very own ‘First Lady of the Lens,’ Homai Vyarawalla.', 'Photography, photography day, learn photography online, women with camera, lady photographer', 'This World Photography Day, NatyaSutraOnline honors India’s very own ‘First Lady of the Lens,’ Homai Vyarawalla.'),
(37, 'Thiruvathira Paattukal', 1, 'n', NULL, '<p>Thiruvathira Paattukal is a unique collection of folk hits that celebrates the southern festival of Thiruvathira.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The highlight of the festivities is a mesmerizing dance, which usually occurs in the Malayalam month of Dhanu. An anthology of classic hits perfectly compliments this carnival of fidelity and communal harmony. NatyaSutraOnline is proud to provide a dedicated background album with tracks that perfectly set the tone for this auspicious period.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Listen to the collection now: <a href=\"https://www.natyasutraonline.com/music/classical-vocal/k-r-shyama/thiruvathira-songs\">Thiruvathira Paattukal</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>ARTIST INFO</strong><br>\r\nComposer and Singer: K. R Shyama<br>\r\nGroup singers: Athira Murali, Saranya B Nair, Rajalakshmi R. S<br>\r\nTabla and idakka: Hari Krishnamurthy</p>', NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, '', NULL, 'thiruvathira-paattukal.jpg', '', 'Thiruvathira Paattukal', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, '2021-08-18 13:44:50', 4, '27.62.5.84', '2023-06-13 05:22:50', 10, '49.37.235.73', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'thiruvathira-paattukal', 'Thiruvathira Paattukal', 'Thiruvathira Paattukal, Onam songs, Onam', 'Thiruvathira Paattukal is a unique collection of folk hits that celebrates the southern festival of Thiruvathira.'),
(38, 'Kanden Kanden Sitaye... Mohiniyattam Workshop', 1, 'n', NULL, '<p>NatyaSutraOnline presents a Mohiniyattam workshop with Smt. Smitha Rajan, celebrating a pivotal piece from the Ramayana.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The composition focuses on showcasing the plethora of emotions that each character experiences amidst a challenging course of events. The Guru guides all enthusiasts with technical demonstrations for each facet of the presentation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Date:</strong> 23rd & 24th October, 2021<br>\r\n<strong>Time:</strong> 6 to 8 PM IST<br>\r\n<strong>Language:</strong> English</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\n6.40 minutes audio will be provided on the second day of the workshop.<br>\r\nZoom Link will be shared on the day of the workshop.<br>\r\nParticipation certificate will be provided.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.natyasutraonline.com/online-workshop/smitha-rajan/kanden-kanden-sitaye\">Click here to register. </a> </p>', NULL, NULL, 19, 77, 'd', NULL, 'kanden-kanden-sitaye-mohiniyattam-workshop.jpg', NULL, 'Kanden Kanden Sitaye... Mohiniyattam Workshop', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '2021-09-23 13:08:52', 4, '61.2.215.254', '2021-10-20 10:08:55', 4, '49.37.181.100', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'kanden-kanden-sitaye', 'Kanden Kanden Sitaye | Mohiniyattam Workshop', 'Mohiniyattam workshop latest updates, zoom class for Mohiniyattam dancers, Mohiniyattam dance compositions, Learn Mohiniyattam online, Dance workshop', 'Mohiniyattam workshop latest updates, zoom class for Mohiniyattam dancers, Mohiniyattam dance compositions, Learn Mohiniyattam online, Dance workshop'),
(39, 'NatyaSutraOnline turns two!', 1, 'n', NULL, '<p><b>#NatyaSutraDanciversary</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p>A new year, a fresh anniversary, and yet another chance to get the band back together. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>This November 1st, we celebrate the 2nd edition of NatyaSutraOnline&#39;s inception. <br>\r\nThis event is a yearly reminder that our amazing global dance community has propelled NatyaSutra to greater heights. The new courses, art forms, and maestros under the NatyaSutra umbrella are testament to this support.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>We have a month of exclusive events to commemorate NatyaSutraOnline turning two. Like last year, considering global circumstances, the event will be hosted virtually. We request the NatyaSutra community to send their video clips documenting their journey in nritya alongside us. All submissions are welcome, be it snippets of your personal development or moves you learned over the last year. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Join us in our month-long Virtual Danciversary Celebration</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>All you have to do is:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Record your classical dance/music performances,</li>\r\n <li>Post it on your social, tag us and use #NatyaSutraDanciversary or mail us at natyasutraonline@gmail.com</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>This Danciversary is our heartfelt tribute to every member of the NatyaSutraOnline family, and we wish to honor its diversity and skill throughout these festivities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/natyasutraonline/\">Facebook</a> | <a href=\"http://www.instagram.com/natyasutraonline\">Instagram</a> | <a href=\"https://twitter.com/NatyaSutra\">Twitter </a>| <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCi1SsvD-VWFv3g2yoZ1pQSw\">YouTube</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>', NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, '', NULL, 'natyasutraonline-turns-two.jpg', NULL, 'NatyaSutraOnline turns two!', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, '2021-10-20 09:59:30', 4, '49.37.181.100', '2022-05-18 14:20:16', 1, '116.68.77.213', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'nso-2nd-anniversary', 'NatyaSutraOnline turns two!', 'Anniversary, dance, classical dance, indian classical art forms, elearning, workshop, tutorials', 'A new year, a fresh anniversary, and yet another chance to get the band back together for the second time!'),
(40, 'Making the move for passion and change', 2, 'n', NULL, '', NULL, NULL, 28, 81, 'd', NULL, 'making-the-move-for-passion-and-change.jpg', NULL, 'Making the move for passion and change', '2021-12-09', 'The New Indian Express', 'Neena-Prasad-News.pdf', 'https://www.newindianexpress.com/cities/kochi/2021/dec/09/making-the-move-for-passion-and-change-2393359.html', 2, 1, '2021-12-10 09:13:37', 10, '202.88.244.195', '2022-05-20 18:10:26', 1, '116.68.74.104', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(41, 'Mohiniyattam Lessons by Dr.Neena Prasad', 1, 'n', NULL, '<p>NatyaSutra’s newest offering is Guru Neena Prasad teaching students the Ananda Bhairavi Swarajathi. Swarajathi is a Carnatic musical composition in Mohiniyattam that is lyrical in nature. Swarajathis are usually devotional and often speak about the courage and triumph of the deity. Ananda Bhairavi Swarajathi is simple but has complexities in its rhythm. Dr. Neena Prasaad teaches the students individual components of each part of composition and elaborates on the performance&#39;s technical aspects.  The learner here is Guru Neena Prasad&#39;s disciple Thomas Vo Van Tao, who hails from France. Bringing his own masculine charm to a traditionally feminine art form, Thoma&#39;s Swarajathi performance guides the learners through the nuances of this classical composition..</p>', NULL, NULL, 28, 81, 'd', NULL, 'mohiniyattam-lessons-by-dr-neena-prasad.jpg', NULL, 'Mohiniyattam Lessons by Dr.Neena Prasad', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, '2022-05-18 14:27:06', 1, '116.68.77.213', '2023-02-24 07:22:49', 1, '61.2.215.254', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'mohiniyattam-lessons-by-dr-neena-prasad', 'Mohiniyattam Lessons by Dr. Neena Prasad', 'Mohiniyattam Lessons, Dr. Neena Prasad, Mohiniyattam , Ananda Bhairavi Swarajathi', 'NatyaSutra’s newest offering is Guru Neena Prasad teaching students the Ananda Bhairavi Swarajathi. The Guru introduces the learners to the nuances of this classical treatise.'),
