(35, 'Classic Ragas', 0, 0, 'f', 'y', 'y', 'Carnatic music album by  vocalist Renjith Rajasekharan. The collection embodies the soul of traditional Indian classical compositions.', '<p>This is a Carnatic music concert by  vocalist Renjith Rajasekharan. Consisting of thirteen melodious kirtanas, each presented in a riveting manner. The collection embodies the soul of traditional Indian classical compositions.</p><p>Violin: A. Jayadevan<br>Mridangam: Cherthala G. Krishnakumar<br>Ghatam : Vazhapally R. Krishnakumar<br>Morsing: Kottayam Murali<br></p>', 'renjith-songs.jpg', 'renjith-songs.jpg', 'renjith-songs.jpg', 'Carnatic Vocal', '2020-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'classic-ragas', 'Listen to Carnatic Music Concert, Ten Melodious Kirtanas, by Renjith Rajasekharan,', 'carnatic vocal, carnatic music download, free carnatic vocal, online carnatic music , carnatic raga-based songs,classical music vocal,indian classical music,indian classical music ragas,carnatic music, song lyrics in kannada,brochevaru meaning in english,khamas raga,khamas raga film songs,khamas raga alapana,khamas raga kritis, free mp3 download, best free mp3 download sites, free playlist download mp3, mp3 album download, direct download mp3 songs, best mp3 song download', 'Carnatic music album by  vocalist Renjith Rajasekharan. The collection embodies the soul of traditional Indian classical compositions.', '2020-06-20 08:23:06', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2021-09-23 09:51:43', 10, '202.88.244.195', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(36, 'Indian Serenades', 0, NULL, 'p', 'y', 'y', 'Indian Serenades, Flute recital, is a fine example of exquisite music that soothes your soul. Experience it to believe it!', '<p>The tunes of India touch the chords of our hearts. Stringing the aspirations of a people, they waft through in the wind - melodious and ecstatic… Indian Serenades  - Flute recital by Padmesh brings to you the music seeped in the culture of a land, ditties of a bygone era, notes echoing the shimmering green of the woods and pastures.<br><br></p>', 'indian-serenades.jpg', 'indian-serenades.jpg', 'indian-serenades.jpg', 'Flute', '2020-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'indian-serenades', 'Indian Serenades, melodious and ecstatic flute recital,', 'Indian Serenades, padmesh, flute, Flute Recital,Flute Music,Padmesh,indian flute instrumental music free download,flute music indian,flute music audio,flute music - youtube,best flute music,relaxing music,flute music,Music ,flute types,flute for beginners,flute sound, free music, indian classical music, free classical music downloads, free download most popular classical music, classical music songs, classical music for studying, classical musical instrument,musical instrument, invis multimedia,\r\nfree mp3 download, best free mp3 download sites, free playlist download mp3, mp3 album download, direct download mp3 songs, best mp3 song download', 'Indian Serenades, Flute recital, is a fine example of exquisite music that soothes your soul. Experience it to believe it!', '2020-06-24 09:09:55', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2020-08-23 08:48:17', 1, '117.230.138.62', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(37, 'Nalacharitham Attakatha Complete', 0, NULL, 'p', 'y', 'y', 'Nalacharitham Attakatha by Kottakkal Madhu  brings the beautiful love story of Nalan and Damayanthi. Attakatha is the literary and lyrical component of the Kathakali performance.  The Nalacharitham Attakatha written by Unnayi Variyar is believed to be one of the gems in this genre.', '<p>Nalacharitham Attakatha Complete (Full Text) brings to you the events that unfold on the 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 4th acts of the love story. First two acts takes you through right from when Nalan is smitten with Damayanthi to the point where they are separated owing to the jealousy of Kali. 3rd and 4th acts of the story unveils before the audience events from the time in which Nalan is forced into disguise after being bitten by a serpent to how Damayanthi recognizes Nalan and their union in the end.<br><br>Vocal: Kottakkal Madhu, Kalanilayam Rajeevan, Vengeri Narayanan<br>Chenda: Kalamandalam Krishnadas<br>Maddalam: Margi Ratnakaran <br></p><p>The love story of Nala and Damayanthi narrated in the Aranya Parvam section of the great Indian epic, The Mahabharatha is an evergreen classic. Attakatha is the literary and lyrical component of the Kathakali performance. The Nalacharitham Attakatha written by Unnayi Variyar (17th century CE) is widely believed to be one of the gems in this genre. <br></p>', 'nalacharitham-attakatha.jpg', 'nalacharitham-attakatha.jpg', 'nalacharitham-attakatha.jpg', 'Nalacharitham Kathakali', '2014-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'nalacharitham-attakatha', 'Nalacharitham Attakatha, Complete Kathakali Text  sung by Kottakkal Madhu', 'nalacharitham, attakatha, kathakali, nalacharitham attakatha,dance drama,Kottakkal Madhu, kottakkal madhu songs, kottakkal madhu kathakali padam mp3 download, unnayi warrier,nalacharitham first day,mahabharata,Aranya Parvam,nala,damayanthi,kathakali padam lyrics,kathakali padam kottackal madhu,nalacharitham kathakali songs,kathakali padam nalacharitham,kottackal madhu kathakali padam mp3, നളചരിതം', 'Nalacharitham Attakatha by Kottakkal Madhu  brings the beautiful love story of Nalan and Damayanthi. Attakatha is the literary and lyrical component of the Kathakali performance.  The Nalacharitham Attakatha written by Unnayi Variyar is believed to be one of the gems in this genre.', '2020-06-25 08:14:16', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2020-12-11 14:16:37', 1, '117.230.32.65', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(38, 'Narayaneeyam', 0, 1, 'f', 'y', 'y', 'Narayaneeyam mp3s online for free download.   Hear the audios of  25 dasakams of Narayaneeyam chanting by Dr. Rajashree Warrier.', '<p>\r\n\r\nMusic and Vocal : Dr. Rajashree Warrier<br>Veena : Prof. V. Soundararajan </p><p>The sacred verses of the Narayaneeyam, exalting the virtues of Lord Krishna, are now streaming on NatyaSutraOnline. These 25 dasakams or audio tracks are the handiwork of celebrated Dancer and Musician, Dr. Rajashree Warrier. Her melodious vocals reinvigorate these divine tones and serenade the soul of each listener.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>', 'narayaneeyam1.jpg', 'narayaneeyam1.jpg', 'narayaneeyam1.jpg', 'Narayaneeyam', '2020-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'narayaneeyam', 'Narayaneeyam  Recital,  Free Audio Download | Dr. Rajashree Warrier | First 25 dasakams of the sacred verse', 'Narayaneeyam, sriman narayaneeyam, narayaneeyam with meaning, narayaneeyam mp3, narayaneeyam for beginners, narayaneeyam commentary, rajashree warrier, narayaneeyam free online classes, narayaneeyam free download mp3, narayaneeyam audio free download, narayaneeyam full mp3 download, narayaneeyam pdf, narayaneeyam sanskrit pdf, narayaneeyam chanting for beginners, narayaneeyam parayanam at home, narayaneeyam chanting procedure, narayaneeyam chanting benefits, narayaneeyam chanting audio, narayaneeyam slokas, narayaneeyam online', 'Narayaneeyam mp3s online for free download.   Hear the audios of  25 dasakams of Narayaneeyam chanting by Dr. Rajashree Warrier. Narayaneeyam, exalting the virtues of Lord Krishna, are now streaming on NatyaSutraOnline.', '2020-07-07 11:14:38', 1, '137.97.175.73', '2023-09-05 14:14:56', 1, '49.37.235.51', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(39, 'Jayadevan Solo', 0, NULL, 'p', 'y', 'y', 'The Music album contains ten tracks, all violin covers of famous Indian classical compositions. These performances also provide background instruments, including Mridangam and Ghatam.', '<p>This album is a ten-song collection by renowned violinist, Jayadevan. The music covers the length and breadth of Indian classical music’s ethos, with some of the pioneers being paid homage in the artisan’s unique way. Listeners are serenaded with pieces that were initially penned by the greats, including Swathi Thirunal, Thyagaraja, and Dayananda Saraswathi. It is the perfect modern interpretation of these iconic compositions.  Original writers whose work is referenced include Veenai Koopaiyer, Lalitha Dasar, Arulavan, Sadashiva Brahmendra, Bharathiyar & Jayadeva, and Dr. M. Balamuralikrishna.<br><br>Violin: Jayadevan<br>Mridangam: Neiveli Venkatesh <br>Ghatam: Thripunithura Radhakrishnan <br></p>', 'jayadevan-solo.jpg', 'jayadevan-solo.jpg', 'jayadevan-solo.jpg', 'violin', '2020-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'jayadevan-solo', 'This Violin Solo emanates from the bow of maestro Jayadevan, a leading figure in Carnatic and Western Music.', 'violin, violin solo classical, romantic violin classical music, violin music,  beautiful violin music, violin music mp3, violin music tamil, classical, carnatic classical music, karnatic, concert, recital,jayadevan, mrudangam, Mridangam, Neiveli Venkatesh, Ghatam, Thripunithura Radhakrishnan, Swathi Thirunal, Thyagaraja, Dayananda Saraswathi, Indian classical compositions, Veenai Koopaiyer, Lalitha Dasar, Arulavan, Sadashiva Brahmendra, Bharathiyar, Balamuralikrishna', 'The Music album contains ten tracks, all violin covers of famous Indian classical compositions. These performances also provide background instruments, including Mridangam and Ghatam.', '2020-07-23 10:58:47', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2020-08-23 08:46:22', 1, '117.230.138.62', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(40, 'Flute Recital', 0, NULL, 'p', 'y', 'y', 'The entire album contains eight tracks, all flute renditions of famous Indian classical compositions. Original writers of these works include Purandara Dasa, Oothukadu Venkatasurba Kavi Rayar, Sri Bhadrachala Ramadasa, Lalgudi Jayaraman, and Arunagiri Nadhar.', '<p>This album is an eight-song compilation by celebrated flutist, Chandan Kumar. The music encompasses every facet of traditional Indian classical music, with the artisan paying homage to some of the giants of craft. The public gets to enjoy pieces written by stalwarts of Indian culture, including Thyagaraja, G. N. Balasubramanian, and K. Vasudevacharya. It is a 21st-century take on ageless classics. <br></p>', 'mysore-chandan-kumar.jpg', 'mysore-chandan-kumar.jpg', 'mysore-chandan-kumar.jpg', 'flute', '2020-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'flute-renditions', 'Flute renditions of famous Indian classical compositions by Mysore Chandan Kumar', 'Mysore Chandan Kumar, flute, Flute Recital,Flute Music,indian flute instrumental music free download,flute music indian,flute music audio,flute music - youtube,best flute music,relaxing music,flute music,Music ,flute types,flute for beginners,flute sound, free music, indian classical music, free classical music downloads, free download most popular classical music, classical music songs, classical music for studying, classical musical instrument,musical instrument, invis multimedia,', 'The entire album contains eight tracks, all flute renditions of famous Indian classical compositions. Original writers of these works include Purandara Dasa, Oothukadu Venkatasurba Kavi Rayar, Sri Bhadrachala Ramadasa, Lalgudi Jayaraman, and Arunagiri Nadhar.', '2020-07-23 10:59:06', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2020-08-23 08:45:38', 1, '117.230.138.62', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(41, 'Rajasthani Jugalbandhi', 0, 1, 'f', 'y', 'y', 'Jugalbandhi is usually performed during Rajasthani wedding ceremonies and other auspicious occasions.   Most of the Rajasthani folk dances are accompanied by instruments, namely, Dholak, Kadthal, Nagara and Morchang.', '<p>\r\n\r\nMost of the Rajasthani folk dances are accompanied by instruments, namely, Dholak, Kadthal, Nagara and Morchang. Dholak, Nagara and Kadthal are percussion instruments, while Morching is a string instrument. Jugalbandhi is a musical ensemble in which all the aforementioned instruments are played together. Jugalbandhi is usually performed during Rajasthani wedding ceremonies and other auspicious occasions.\r\n\r\n<br></p><p>\r\n\r\nNimbuda Nimbuda\" is one of the most popular folk songs from Rajasthan. It is sung during the weddings and other ceremonies. The musicians are dressed in white dhotis and kurtas with their heads  embellished with colourful, oversized turbans.\r\n\r\n<br></p>', 'rajasthani-jugalbandhi.jpg', 'rajasthani-jugalbandhi.jpg', 'rajasthani-jugalbandhi.jpg', 'Rajasthani  Musicians singing folk ', '2010-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'rajasthani-jugalbandhi', 'Rajasthani Jugalbandhi ( Musical Ensemble ) | Rajasthani Folk Music', 'Jugalbandhi, Rajasthani Folk Music, MusicalEnsemble,  dholak, morching, percussion instruments, rajasthani wedding,  Nimbuda Nimbuda,  Indian Folk Musc,  traditional rajasthani folk music, indian music, folk song', 'Jugalbandhi is usually performed during Rajasthani wedding ceremonies and other auspicious occasions.   Most of the Rajasthani folk dances are accompanied by instruments, namely, Dholak, Kadthal, Nagara and Morchang.', '2021-03-04 10:19:48', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2021-06-06 16:24:54', 1, '116.68.76.228', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(42, 'Adhyathma Ramayanam Kilippattu', 0, 1, 'f', 'y', 'y', 'Adhyathma Ramayanam Kilippattu,  famous rendition of the Ramayana in Kerala. This entire recital in Malayalam and is sung by Smt Meera Rammohan and contains six distinct chapters or kandams. These are : Balakandam, Ayodhyakandam, Aranyakandam, Kishkintakandam, Sundarakandam and Yudhakandam.', '<p>This audio recording tells the story of the Ramayana, a famous Indian epic, in a version in Malayalam language called Adhyathma Ramayanam Kilippattu. It was written by Thunchaththu Ramanujan Ezhuthachan in the 17th century. He gave it a regional twist based on the Vedic interpretation of the original Ramayana called Adhyatma Ramayana. The story is told and has six chapters: Balakandam, Ayodhyakandam, Aranyakandam, Kishkintakandam, Sundarakandam and Yudhakandam.   In Kerala, people recities this during the month of Karkitakam, which falls during July and August.<br><br>The Ramayana has been cherished by people in India for generations.  It was written by Sage Valmiki between the 7th and 4th centuries BCE. The story is set in the Treta Yuga and follows the tale of the legendary Lord Rama, the seventh avatar of Lord Vishnu. Rama\'s simplicity, virtuous nature, and courage make his journey relatable to ordinary people. The story highlights themes of courage, love, and family bonds that resonate across cultures and unify the sub-continent.<br></p>', 'അദധയതമ-രമയണ3.jpg', 'അദധയതമ-രമയണ4.jpg', 'അദധയതമ-രമയണ7.jpg', 'Ramayanam Malayalam', '2021-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'adhyatma-ramayanam-malayalam', 'Adhyathma Ramayanam Kilippattu | Full Ramayana Recital in Malayalam Free Audio MP3', 'Adhyatma Ramayana,adhyatma ramayanam malayalam,ramayanam in malayalam, adhyathma ramayanam kilippattu malayalam lyrics, adhyatma ramayanam kilippattu malayalam free download, bala kanda slokas, ramayanam mp3 songs download, ramayanam malayalam full mp3 free download,  sampoorna ramayanam malayalam mp3 songs free download, Ramayanam Malayalam Audio, രാമായണം പാരായണം, രാമായണം കഥ,രാമായണം വരികൾ,താരോപദേശം രാമായണം,അദ്ധ്യാത്മ രാമായണം, hindu devotional songs mp3 download, malayalam devotional mp3 songs free download, valmiki ramayana audio malayalam, valmiki ramayana chanting mp3, valmiki ramayanam malayalam pdf free download', 'Adhyathma Ramayanam Kilippattu,  famous rendition of the Ramayana in Kerala. This entire recital in Malayalam and is sung by Smt Meera Rammohan and contains six distinct chapters or kandams. These are : Balakandam, Ayodhyakandam, Aranyakandam, Kishkintakandam, Sundarakandam and Yudhakandam.', '2021-07-19 09:39:03', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2025-08-18 08:31:04', 19, '49.37.232.247', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(43, 'Thiruvathirappattukal', 0, 1, 'p', 'y', 'y', 'Traditional Thiruvathira songs in Malayalam.  Thiruvathira pattukal is the song that accompanies Thiruvathirakali or Thiruvathira dance', '<p>Music composed and sung by : K.R Shyama<br>Group singers: Athira Murali, Saranya B Nair, Rajalakshmi.R.S<br>Tabla and idakka: Hari Krishnamurthy<br><br>ഇതിൽ \r\n\r\nപതിനൊന്ന് \r\n\r\nതിരുവാതിരപ്പാട്ടുകൾ  ഉൾപ്പെടുന്നു. <br><br>ഗണപതേ മാം പാലയ (ഗണപതി സ്തുതി)<br>പാലായ പാപ ഹരേ (സരസ്വതി സ്തുതി)<br>നന്ദ നന്ദനൻ ഗോവിന്ദൻ (തിരുവാതിര)<br>മതി മായ കശ്യപനോ (കുമ്മി)<br>ജയ ജയ കരിവദന (ഗണപതി സ്തുതി)<br>സിന്ധു വാരമേ കുന്ദ ജാലമേ (തിരുവാതിര)<br>പച്ചക്കല്ലോത്ത തിരുമേനിയും (കുമ്മി)<br>ആലുവ തേവാരെ (വഞ്ചി പാട്ട്)<br>വെള്ളപ്പുടവ ഉടുതും കൊണ്ടും (കുറത്തി പാട്ട്)<br>\r\n\r\nമല്ല വൈരി പാദ പദമം \r\n\r\n (കുമ്മി)\r\n\r\n<br>മംഗളം<br></p><p>\r\n\r\nThiruvathira pattukal sung during the occasion of Thiruvathira celebrated on the Thiruvathira asterism in the Malayalam month of Dhanu (December/January). Thiruvathira pattukal is the song that accompanies Thiruvathirakali.<br>\r\n\r\n<br></p>', 'thiruvathirappattukal2.jpg', 'thiruvathirappattukal2.jpg', 'thiruvathirappattukal2.jpg', 'thiruvathira-songs', '2021-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'thiruvathira-songs', 'തിരുവാതിരപ്പാട്ടുകൾ | Traditional Thiruvathira songs in Malayalam', 'തിരുവാതിരപ്പാട്ടുകൾ, thiruvathira pattukal lyrics in malayalam, traditional thiruvathira songs, thiruvathira nakshatra, thiruvathira dance, thiruvathira kummi songs lyrics, thiruvathira songs mp3 free download, malayalam thiruvathira, Thiruvathirapattu, Thiruvathira Songs Lyrics in Malayalam pdf, Aavani Thiruvathira Songs mp3 free download, Thiruvathirakali, Thiruvathira songs in Malayalam films', 'Traditional Thiruvathira songs in Malayalam.  Thiruvathira pattukal is the song that accompanies Thiruvathirakali or Thiruvathira dance', '2021-08-09 13:15:00', 1, '117.232.108.17', '2026-10-19 02:48:11', 19, '49.37.232.76', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0),
(44, 'Keraleeyam', 0, 1, 'p', 'y', 'y', 'Keraleeyam,  Kerala  Music by Sreevalsan J. Menon is a complete slice of God’s Own Country for all classical and folk music enthusiasts.', '<p>Keraleeyam is a complete slice of God’s Own Country for all classical and folk music enthusiasts. From the eastern peaks to the western coast, this album encompasses every aspect of the state’s musical ethos. The nine tracks in this compilation romanticize the various geographical tones that truly define what the coastal state represents. These handpicked tunes are meticulously composed, using a wide array of instruments, both traditional and modern. Keraleeyam is your de facto introduction to the masterpiece that is Kerala.<br><br>ARTIST INFO<br><br>Music        -  Sreevalsan J menon<br>Violin        -  Jay Nair <br>Associate Composer    -  Edappilly Ajithkumar<br>Programmer      -  Anil.K.K<br>Guitar        -  Sangeeth Pavithran<br>Mridangam      -  Balakrishna Kammath<br>Wind        -  Rison<br>Voices        -  Amal Antony, Meera Ram Mohan<br>Mix down      -  Rajan Francis, Chetana Sound Studios, Thrissur<br>Recorded and Mastered by  -  Saji.R.Nair, Chetana Sound Studios, Thrissur<br><br></p>', 'keraleeyam.jpg', 'keraleeyam.jpg', 'keraleeyam.jpg', 'Keraleeyam', '2021-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'keraleeyam', 'Keraleeyam, Kerala Music by Sreevalsan J. Menon and Violin by Jayadevan', 'Keraleeyam, Kerala, Sreevalsan J. Menon, kerala music, music of kerala, kerala music ringtone, kerala music mp3 free download, sreevalsan j menon songs, sreevalsan j menon, sreevalsan j menon songs mp3 free download, jayadevan, violin, kerala music instruments, kerala traditional music, famous music of kerala, folk music of kerala, kerala traditional background music', 'Keraleeyam,  Kerala  Music by Sreevalsan J. Menon is a complete slice of God’s Own Country for all classical and folk music enthusiasts.', '2021-09-03 06:11:09', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2026-05-21 17:47:14', 19, '49.37.226.138', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0),
(45, 'Varsha Parvam', 0, 0, 'p', 'y', 'y', '', '', '', '', '', '', '2021-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '', '', '2021-09-03 06:11:50', 1, '202.88.244.195', '2021-09-03 09:13:04', 10, '202.88.244.195', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0),
(46, 'Raga Series', 0, 0, 'f', 'y', 'y', 'A 20-lesson raga series on veena by Jayalakshmi Sekhar, trained under the guidance of Dr. Pinakapani, and recognized as a leading exponent of the veena in the Carnatic tradition.', '<p>This course presents a raga series of Carnatic instrumental music performed on the veena by Jayalakshmi Sekhar, a versatile musician from a family of musicians, trained under the guidance of Dr. Pinakapani, and recognized as a leading exponent of the veena in the Carnatic tradition.<br><br>Spread across 20 lessons, the series covers ragas including <br></p><ol><li>Saveri</li><li>Sahana</li><li>Neelambari</li><li>Ranjini</li><li>Poorvikalyani</li><li>Pantuvarali</li><li>Nalinakanthi</li><li>Navarasa</li><li>Keeravani</li><li>Kedaragowla</li><li>Kambhoji</li><li>Kannada</li><li>Hamsanadam</li><li>Garudadhvani</li><li>Bilahari</li><li>Andolika</li><li>Thodi</li><li>Vachaspati</li><li>Sreeranjini</li><li>Neelambari</li></ol>Each raga is presented through a full recital featuring a composition set to a classical tala, with several lessons accompanied by a shorter companion clip highlighting the raga\'s melodic character. For listeners and learners alike, this series offers both an immersive listening experience and a clear, unhurried window into the expressive range of Carnatic music on the veena.<br><br>Jayalakshmi Sekhar is a Chennai-based veena maestro. She has been honoured with the Veena award from Narada Gana Sabha, the Gana Kala Shiromani title, and lifetime achievement awards from Malaysia and Australia. She is currently empanelled by the Indian Council for Cultural Relations and has performed widely across India and internationally over a concert career spanning several decades.<br><p></p>', 'raga-series-veena-recital-by-jayalakshmi-sekhar.webp', '', 'raga-series-veena-recital-by-jayalakshmi-sekhar.webp', 'Veena', '2026-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'raga-series', 'Carnatic Music Raga Lessons | Veena Recital by Jayalakshmi Sekhar | Natyasutra', 'Carnatic veena lessons online, veena raga series, jayalakshmi sekhar veena, learn carnatic music online, classical veena course, carnatic instrumental music, veena recital India, andholika raga veena, kambhoji veena, natyasutra music, carnatic raga series', 'A 20-lesson raga series on veena by Jayalakshmi Sekhar, covering fourteen Carnatic ragas including Andholika, Kambhoji, Neelambari, Sahana, and Saveri. Explore Carnatic instrumental music with a leading exponent of the veena.', '2026-05-19 07:44:01', 19, '49.37.224.200', '2026-05-19 11:40:56', 19, '49.37.224.200', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(47, 'Raga Series', 0, 0, 'f', 'y', 'n', '', '<p>This course presents Carnatic music performed on the violin by A. Jayadevan. Across 32 lessons, maestro Jayadevan renders a selection of Carnatic ragas, each presented as a focused solo recital that draws out the distinct melodic character of the raga. The series covers ragas including :</p><p><br>1.  Nata<br>2.  Bhoopalam<br>3.  Bhoopalam<br>4.  Bihag<br>5.  Bindumalini<br>6.  Desakshi<br>7.  Hamir Kalyani<br>8.  Jayamanohari<br>9.  Kapi<br>10.  Manorama<br>11.  Saranga<br>12.  Sivaranjini <br>13.  Vasanthi<br>14.  Vijayanagari<br>15.  Sindhuramakriya<br>16.  Patdeep<br>17.  Mohanam<br>18.  Kuntalavarali<br>19.  Rathipathipriya<br>20.  Brindavani<br>21.  Chandrajyoti<br>22.  Ragavarthini<br>23.  Agnikopam<br>24.  Malahari<br>25.  Neelambari<br>26.  Mohananagi<br>27.  Suryakanthi<br>28.  Maand<br>29.  Khamas<br>30.  Surya<br>31.  Desh<br>32.  Shuddha Seemanthini<br><br>A. Jayadevan is an Indian-born Canadian violinist who hails from a family of artistes, with his grandfather Abhayadev being a well-known name in both the Malayalam film and literary worlds. One of the true ambassadors of traditional Indian music in Canada, he is adept across Indian classical, fusion, and western music.<br></p>', 'raga-series.webp', '', 'raga-series.webp', 'Violin', '2026-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'raga-series-violin', 'Carnatic Music Raga Lessons | Violin Recital by A. Jayadevan | Natyasutra', 'carnatic violin lessons online, violin raga series, a. jayadevan violin, raga prapancham, carnatic instrumental music, learn carnatic music online, classical violin india, carnatic raga recital, natyasutra music, violin carnatic ragas', 'A raga series of Carnatic violin recitals by A. Jayadevan. Part of the Raga Prapancham series on Natyasutra, exploring individual ragas through solo instrumental performance.', '2026-05-23 04:57:31', 19, '49.37.226.252', '2026-05-23 05:25:29', 19, '49.37.226.252', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(48, 'Melam', 0, 1, 'f', 'y', 'y', 'A Unique Kerala Percussion Ensemble of Mizhavu, Thimila and Edakka', '<p>The resonating yet captivating beat of the percussion instrument, Mizhavu, gives rhythm and strikes the right mood for actors to express their body language and facial expressions. Mizhavu is an integral part of Koothu and Kutiyattam, the millennia old performing art forms of Kerala. The video titled Melam features a rare ensemble of Mizhavu with two other percussion instruments viz. Thimila and Edakka. Both Thimila and Edakka are part of Panchavadyam, the traditional orchestra of Kerala. These videos are available in SD quality only.<br><br>Thimila   : Margi Mohanan<br>Mizhavu   : Margi Ramanunni<br>Edakka     : Margi Subramanian Potti<br>Elathalam : Margi Sathi<br></p>', 'melam.jpg', 'melam.jpg', 'melam.jpg', '', '2020-01-01', NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'melam-percussion-ensemble-mizhavu-thimila-edakka', 'Mizhavu, Thimila & Edakka Ensemble: Traditional Kerala Percussion | Melam', 'Mizhavu, Thimila, Edakka, Melam video, Kerala percussion instruments, Kutiyattam music, Koothu orchestra, Panchavadyam instruments, traditional Kerala melam, SD percussion video', 'Experience Melam, a rare Kerala percussion ensemble featuring Mizhavu, Thimila, and Edakka. Discover the captivating rhythms of Kutiyattam and Panchavadyam in SD quality.', '2026-11-03 07:56:43', 19, '49.37.233.110', '2026-11-05 06:50:38', 19, '49.37.235.16', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1);
