(6, 'Kerala Folk Art Forms', 0, 'y', '2022-10-27', NULL, 'Explore the cultural richness of a population and its amazing diversities through a tour of Kerala\'s folk art forms. You would enjoy the rhythmic steps and captivating music that unveil old myths, folklores, customs and practices unique to the differ', '<p>Explore the cultural richness of a population and its amazing diversities through a tour of Kerala&#39;s folk art forms. You would enjoy the rhythmic steps and captivating music that unveil old myths, folklores, customs and practices unique to the different communities and regions of this land. Almost all events of a human life are occasions to celebrate in God&#39;s Own Country.<br>\r\n </p>\r\n', 0, 'g', 34, 'kerala-folk-art-forms', 'Folk and Tribal Art Forms of Kerala | Musical instruments, Costume, History & Origin', 'Folk art forms, Folk art forms of Kerala, folk arts of kerala, art forms of kerala malayalam, art forms of kerala introduction, performing arts of kerala,  art of kerala, Kakkarissi Natakam, Kothamooriyattam, Mudiyattam, Poothanum Thirayum, Thirayattam, Gaddika, Alamikkali, Mangalamkali', 'Explore the cultural richness of a population and its amazing diversities through a tour of Kerala\'s folk art forms. You would enjoy the rhythmic steps and captivating music that unveil old myths, folklores, customs and practices unique to the different communities and regions of this land.', 'n', 1, '2022-10-27 05:48:54', '202.88.244.195', 1, '2023-01-02 11:39:58', '49.37.225.38', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(7, 'സംസ്ഥാന തലസ്ഥാനമായ തിരുവനന്തപുരം നഗരത്തില്‍ സ്ഥിതി ചെയ്യുന്ന', 0, 'y', '2022-10-31', NULL, '', '<h5 class=\"text-gray  sub-text \">സംസ്ഥാന തലസ്ഥാനമായ തിരുവനന്തപുരം നഗരത്തില്‍ സ്ഥിതി ചെയ്യുന്ന</h5>\r\n', 0, 'b', 36, 'സസഥന-തലസഥനമയ-തരവനനതപര-നഗരതതല-സഥത-ചയയനന', 'സംസ്ഥാന തലസ്ഥാനമായ തിരുവനന്തപുരം നഗരത്തില്‍ സ്ഥിതി ചെയ്യുന്ന', 'സംസ്ഥാന തലസ്ഥാനമായ തിരുവനന്തപുരം നഗരത്തില്‍ സ്ഥിതി ചെയ്യുന്ന', 'സംസ്ഥാന തലസ്ഥാനമായ തിരുവനന്തപുരം നഗരത്തില്‍ സ്ഥിതി ചെയ്യുന്ന', 'n', 1, '2022-10-31 13:02:56', '202.88.244.195', 1, '2022-10-31 13:03:14', '202.88.244.195', 1, '2022-10-31 13:05:49', '202.88.244.195', 2),
(8, 'International Women\'s Day 2023', 0, 'n', '2023-03-10', NULL, 'Guru Pali Chandra, her disciples, and members of Team Natyasutra decided to honour the most important woman in their life, \'Mother Earth\'. This International Womens Day, they set out to personally clean and replenish their surroundings', '<p>Guru Pali Chandra, her disciples, and members of Team Natyasutra decided to honour the most important woman in their life, &#39;Mother Earth&#39;. This International Womens Day, they set out to personally clean and replenish their surroundings, honouring the role played by Mother Nature in their lives. This spontaneous act played out when the Kathak maestro and her disciples arrived for a production shoot concerning her much-anticipated Gita Govinda rendition.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Guru and the Natyastura team realized that the area needed to be cleaned before they commenced work. It soon transformed into a quest to rid the place of waste over a widespread radius, as the project&#39;s ethos champions an environment-friendly approach at all times. The team&#39;s efforts also drew in an enthusiastic public response, as concerned citizens and Panchayat (local self-government) officials began showing up to lend a hand. International Women&#39;s Day 2023 was transformed into a day to honour the lady who protects us all without bias, Mother Earth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>These outdoor shoots are a part of Guru Pali Chandra&#39;s effort to combine, translate and interpret all 24 songs of poet Jayadeva&#39;s iconic Gita Govinda. This is the first such attempt in modern Indian cultural dance history. The focus on Radha in this project will bring new light to the many complexities and mystiques surrounding her character. </p>\r\n', 1, 'g', 48, 'international-womens-day-2023', '2023 Women\'s Day Celebration', 'Intrenational womensday,  Celebrate, Cleaning, Palichandra', 'This International Womens Day, Pali Chandra, her disciples, and members of Team Natyasutra set out to personally clean and replenish their surroundings, honouring the role played by Mother Nature in their lives.', 'n', 10, '2023-03-10 05:38:08', '61.2.215.254', 10, '2023-03-15 04:35:36', '61.2.215.254', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(9, 'tet gita govinda', 3, 'n', '2023-07-15', NULL, '', '', 0, 'e', 32, 'dfsdfsd', 'sdfsdf', 'sdfsdf', 'sdfsdf', 'n', 1, '2023-07-15 05:54:09', '202.88.244.195', 1, '2023-07-15 05:54:29', '202.88.244.195', 1, '2023-07-15 05:55:32', '202.88.244.195', 2),
(10, 'Asamyuta Hasta', 0, 'n', '2023-08-02', NULL, 'Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand. According to abhinaya darpan there are 28 asamuta hasta mudras.', '<p><span xss=\"removed\"><span xss=\"removed\"><span xss=\"removed\"><span xss=\"removed\"><span xss=\"removed\">Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand. According to abhinaya darpan there are 28 asamuta hasta mudras.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n', 0, 'g', 24, 'asamyuta-hasta-bharatanatyam', 'Asamyuta Hasta | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Hastabhedah or Hand Postures are used to denote various thoughts, ideas and objects. There are  two varieties of hand gestures - Asamyuta Hastas or non-combined and Samyuta Hastas or combined. Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand. According to \'Abhinaya Darpan\' there are 28 asamyuta hasta mudras.', 'n', 16, '2023-08-02 07:11:46', '171.49.216.52', 10, '2023-08-02 07:18:52', '171.49.216.52', 16, '2023-08-02 07:24:23', '171.49.216.52', 2),
(11, 'Asamyuta Hasta', 0, 'n', '2023-08-02', NULL, 'Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand. According to abhinaya darpan there are 28 asamuta hasta mudras.', '<p><span xss=\"removed\"><span xss=\"removed\"><span xss=\"removed\"><span xss=\"removed\"><span xss=\"removed\">Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand. According to abhinaya darpan there are 28 asamuta hasta mudras.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n', 18, 'g', 27, 'asamyuta-hasta-bharatanatyam', 'Asamyuta Hasta | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Hastabhedah or Hand Postures are used to denote various thoughts, ideas and objects. There are  two varieties of hand gestures - Asamyuta Hastas or non-combined and Samyuta Hastas or combined. Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand. According to \'Abhinaya Darpan\' there are 28 asamyuta hasta mudras.', 'n', 16, '2023-08-02 07:12:07', '171.49.216.52', 16, '2023-08-02 07:15:35', '171.49.216.52', 16, '2023-08-02 07:17:11', '171.49.216.52', 2),
(12, 'Asamyuta Hasta Mudras', 0, 'y', '2023-08-02', NULL, 'Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand. According to abhinaya darpan there are 28 asamuta hasta mudras.', '<p>Hastabhedah is defined to be of two varieties - Non-combined or single hand gestures which are called Asamyuta Hasta Mudras and Combined or both hand gestures which are called Samyuta Hasta Mudras.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand. According to Abhinayadarpanam, there are 28 asamyuta hasta mudras. These hand mudras are demonstrated by Dr. Rajashree Warrier.</p>\r\n', 0, 'g', 3, 'asamyuta-hasta-bharatanatyam', 'Asamyuta Hasta Mudras | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras | Gallery', 'asamyuta hasta mudras, single-hand gesture, abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in bharatanatyam, mudras in classical dance, hasta bhedah, hand postures, non-combined hand gestures,  hasta mudras, samyuta hasta, double handed gestures, asamyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Hastabhedah or Hand Postures are used to denote various thoughts, ideas and objects. There are  two varieties of hand gestures - Asamyuta Hastas or non-combined and Samyuta Hastas or combined. Asamyuta hasta mudras or single hand gestures are expressions to be shown by a hand.', 'n', 16, '2023-08-02 07:27:14', '171.49.216.52', 19, '2025-07-18 05:20:43', '49.37.224.171', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(13, 'Samyuta Hasta Mudras', 0, 'y', '2023-10-05', NULL, 'Samyuta Hasta mudras or Combined hand gestures are expressions to be shown by both hands. According to abhinaya darpan there are 23 Samuta hasta mudras.', '<p>Hastabhedah is defined to be of two varieties - Non-combined or single hand gestures which are called Asamyuta Hasta Mudras and Combined or both hand gestures which are called Samyuta Hasta Mudras.  </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Samyuta Hasta mudras or Combined hand gestures are expressions to be shown by both hands. According to abhinaya darpan there are 23 Samyuta hasta mudras. These hand mudras are demonstrated by Dr. Rajashree Warrier.</p>\r\n', 0, 'g', 1, 'samyuta-hasta-bharatanatyam', 'Samyuta Hasta Mudras | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras | Gallery', 'Samyuta Hasta Mudras, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Samyuta Hasta mudras or Combined hand gestures are expressions to be shown by both hands.', 'n', 16, '2023-10-04 09:01:31', '223.184.40.20', 19, '2025-07-18 05:22:33', '49.37.224.171', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1);
