(48, 12, 'Pataka', '<p>Pataka Mudra (flag) is a single-hand gesture, where all fingers are held straight close together and thump is slightly bent. This mudra pose is used at the commencement of natya and to represent the clouds, forest, denial of objects, breasts, night, river, realm of divinities, horse, cutting, wind to decumbent, attempting to go, strength, benefaction, moon-light, fierce heat, opening the doors, in the sense of all sevn case-endings (vibhakti), tides, entering a lane, equanimity, smearing oneself, taking a pledge, silence, palmyra leaf, shield, feeling the objects, blessing, a good king, describing a location, sea, series of meritorious actions, addressing, stepping forward, grasping a sword, month, year, a drizzly day and sweeping with a broom.<br></p>', '112_02082023103416.jpg', '112_02082023103416.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Pataka-Hasta', 'Pataka Hasta Mudra  | Single-Hand Gesture | Classical Dance Mudras', 'Pataka Hasta Mudra, Pataka Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'A single-hand mudra where all the fingers are held straight and close together and thumb is bent.', 0, '2023-08-02 10:34:16', '171.49.216.52', 0, '2024-12-01 17:29:12', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(49, 12, 'Tripataka', '<p>Tripataka Mudra (three parts of the flag) is a single-hand gesture where in from the Pataka pose if the ring finger is bent (almost more than half) and all other fingers are held straight, it is understood to be Tripataka. Tripataka is used to represent a crown, tree, Indra, thunder (Vajrayudha-the weapon of Indra), Ketaki flower, a lamp, flames of fire, a pigeon, putting marks, writing, an arrow and transformation, according to those who knows Natya.<br></p>', '112_02082023110248.jpg', '112_02082023110248.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Tripataka-Hasta', 'Tripataka Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Classical Dance Mudra', 'Tripataka Hasta Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Tripataka Hasta Mudra is single-hand mudra where in the from the pataka if the ring finger is bent.', 0, '2023-08-02 11:02:48', '171.49.216.52', 0, '2024-12-01 17:34:26', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(50, 12, 'Ardhapataka', '<p>\r\n\r\nArdhapataka Mudra is characterised by the bending of the little finger, along with ring finger, in Tripataka Hasta. All other fingers are held straight. Ardhapataka is used to denote leaves, writing/painting board, bank, to mention \'both\', knife, flag, tower, horns and elaboration.</p>', '112_03082023084857.jpg', '112_03082023084857.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Ardhapataka-Hasta', 'Ardhapataka Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Ardhapataka Hasta Mudra, Ardhapataka Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Ardhapataka mudra is a single-hand gesture, characterised by the bending of the little finger along with the ring finger.', 0, '2023-08-03 08:48:58', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2024-12-01 17:33:28', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(51, 12, 'Kartarimukha', '<p>In the Ardhapataka Mudra, if the forefinger and little finger are bent backwards, it is called Kartarimukha. We can also interpret the definition as follows: In the Ardhachandra pose, if the little finger (in the bent position) and the index (in the stretched position) are bent backwards, then, it is Kartarimukha. Kartarimukha Mudra is suitable for depicting parting of a couple, conflicts, opposition, looting, corner of the eye, death, alienating, lightning, sleeping, clever or inconsistency, disjunction, fall, and creeper.</p>', '112_03082023093643.jpg', '112_03082023093643.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Kartarimukha-Hasta', 'Kartarimukha Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bhartanatyam | Mudras', 'Kartarimukha Hasta Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Kartarimukha Hasta Mudra is a single-hand mudra in which from the Ardhpataka pose, the forefinger and the middle finger are bent backwards.', 0, '2023-08-03 09:36:43', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2024-12-01 17:37:23', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(52, 12, 'Mayura', '<p>In Mayura Mudra, the tip of the ring finger and the tip of the thump should touch each other while other fingers are straight touching each other. Mayura Mudra is used in depicting peacock head/neck, creeper, bird, spewing (to throw out), parting of the locks, ornamenting forehead with a mark, dispersing water of rivers or dispersing holy water, knowledge or dialects of scriptural texts and something famous.</p>', '112_03082023095814.jpg', '112_03082023095814.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Mayura-Hasta', 'Mayura Hasta Mudra | SIngle-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Mayura Hasta Mudra, Mayura Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Mayura Hasta Mudra is done with the tip of the ring finger and the tip of the thump touch each other while other fingers are erect and touching each other.', 0, '2023-08-03 09:58:14', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2024-12-01 17:38:56', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(53, 12, 'Ardhachandra', '<p>Ardhachandra Mudra is defined as a pose with thump of Pataka outstretched (all other fingers stretched out and held together to depict the half moon). Ardhachandra is used to depict digit of moon on eighth night during waning fortnight, grabbing and pushing by neck, lance, consecrating and bathing an image, dining vessel, source of origin, waist, contemplating on oneself, meditation, invocation, touching of ones limbs and accosting ordinary people. </p>', '112_03082023120854.jpg', '112_03082023120854.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Ardhacandra-Hasta', 'Ardhachandra Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Ardhachandra Hasta Mudra, Ardhachandra Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Ardhachandra Hasta Mudra is a single-hand mudra which is defined as a pose with thumb of Pataka outstretched (all other fingers stretched out and held together to depict the half moon.', 0, '2023-08-03 12:08:54', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2024-12-01 17:41:11', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(54, 12, 'Arala', '<p>Arala Mudra is a single-hand gesture where in the forefinger of Pataka pose is bent, along with the thump and rest of the fingers are stretched and held together. Arala Mudra denotes drinking venom, nectar, etc. and a violent gale.</p>', '112_04082023075920.jpg', '112_04082023075920.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Arala-Hasta', 'Arala Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras\r\n', 'Arala Hasta Mudra, Arala Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Arala Hasta Mudra is a single-hand mudra where in the forefinger of Pataka pose is bent along with the thump and rest of the fingers are stretched and held together.', 0, '2023-08-04 07:59:20', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2024-12-01 17:42:05', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(55, 12, 'Shukatunda', '<p>Shukatunda Mudra is when the ring finger of Arala is bent. Shukatunda is found utilised in depicting shooting of an arrow, a lance, recollecting ones repose, mystical invocations and outrageous mood.</p>', '112_04082023093548.jpg', '112_04082023093548.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Sukatunda-Hasta', 'Shukatunda Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Shukatunda Hasta Mudra, Sukatunda Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Shukatunda Hasta Mudra is a single-hand mudra in which the ring finger of Arala is bent.', 0, '2023-08-04 09:35:48', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2026-06-02 13:00:10', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(56, 12, 'Mushti', '<p>In Mushti Mudra four fingers are bent and closely pressed towards the palm and thump is placed upon them. Mushti is found applied to depict upright-ness, grouping ones tresses, taking hold of objects and combative posture of wrestlers. </p>', '112_04082023095311.jpg', '112_04082023095311.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Musti-Hasta', 'Mushti Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Mushti Hasta Mudra, Musti Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Mushti Hasta Mudra is a single-hand mudra in which four fingers are bent and closely pressed towards the palm and thump is placed upon them.', 0, '2023-08-04 09:53:11', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2026-06-02 13:01:41', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(57, 12, 'Shikhara', '<p>In Shikhara Mudra, from Mushti, the thump is raised upwards and held straight. It is found used to depict the God of love, bow, column or pillar, surety, offerings to ancestors, offering of cakes to manes, the upper lips, entry of some object, a tooth, interrogation, sivalinga, denying, remembrance, proximity to gestures, drawing of girdle, embrace and ringing a bell.<br></p>', '112_04082023100255.jpg', '112_04082023100255.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Sikhara-Hasta', 'Shikhara Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gestures | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Shikhara Hasta Mudra, Sikhara Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Shikhara Hasta Mudra is a single-hand mudra in which from the Musti pose, the thump is raised upwards and held straight.', 0, '2023-08-04 10:02:55', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2026-06-02 13:03:15', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(58, 12, 'Kapittha', '<p>Bending the forefinger of the Sikhara pose and placing it over the thumb in a pressing position, forms Kapittha pose. Kapittha Mudra is used for representing Lakshmi, Sarasvati, grasping the cymbals, milking the cows, collyrium, holding the flowers during amorous sport, the edge of upper garment, gathering cloth, waving lights or offering incense and fanning. <br></p>', '112_05082023121140.jpg', '112_05082023121140.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Kapittha-Hasta', 'Kapittha Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Kapittha Hasta Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Kapittha Hasta Mudra is a single-hand mudra in which the forefinger of the Sikhara pose and placing it over the thumb in a pressing position.', 0, '2023-08-05 12:11:41', '27.57.7.226', 0, '2024-12-01 17:47:12', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1);
INSERT INTO `tb_picture` (`id`, `pgallery_id`, `p_caption`, `description`, `image_name`, `large_image`, `display_order`, `cover_display`, `file_name`, `page_title`, `meta_keywords`, `meta_description`, `added_by`, `added_on`, `added_by_ip`, `updated_by`, `updated_on`, `updated_by_ip`, `deleted_by`, `deleted_on`, `deleted_by_ip`, `status`) VALUES
(59, 12, 'Katakamukha', '<p>Katakamukha Mudra is defined to be when fore-finger and middle finger of Kapittha are pressed against the thumb, while ring and little finger of Kapittha are to be raised. Katakamukha is preferred to indicate plucking flowers, arrangement and holding garland or necklaces of pearl, etc., pulling the bow-string, offering betel leaves, grinding to paste materials such as musk etc., anointing fragrant material, speaking and gazing.</p>', '112_04092023093514.jpg', '112_04092023093514.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Katakamukha-Hasta', 'Katakamukha Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Katakamukha Hasta Mudra, Katakamukha Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Katakamukha Hasta Mudra is a single hand mudra in which the fore-finger and middle-finger of Kapittha are pressed against the thumb, while ring and little finger of Kapittha are to be raised. ', 0, '2023-09-04 09:35:14', '223.190.214.230', 0, '2024-12-01 17:48:17', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(60, 12, 'Suchi', '<p>In the Katakamukha pose when the forefinger is completely stretched out, it is called Suchi Mudra. Suchi Mudra is preferred to indicate \'One Supreme Brahman\', centum, solar disc, city, the worlds, in sense of supportive statements such as \'may it be\', conditional statements such as \'as-so\', loneliness, threatening, becoming slim, twig, body, amazement, matted locks, umbrella, competency, palms, tresses, beating the drums, circular movement of potter\'s wheel, a disc, enquiry and culmination of the day. </p>', '112_13092023072534.jpg', '112_13092023072534.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Suci-Hasta', 'Suchi Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Suchi Hasta, Suchi Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'In the katakamukha pose when the forefinger is completely stretched out, it is Suchi Mudra.', 0, '2023-09-13 07:25:34', '223.184.62.235', 0, '2024-12-02 02:42:55', '49.37.224.45', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(61, 12, 'Chandrakala', '<p>Release of thumb from Suchi Mudra is Chandrakala Mudra. The application of Chandrakala Mudra is prescribed to indicate moon, face, measurement ie,. the extent between thumb and index finger, the objects of the respective dimension, the crest of Siva, Ganga river and Club (weapon).</p>', '112_13092023114520.jpg', '112_13092023114520.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Candrakala-Hasta', 'Chandrakala Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Chandrakala Hasta Mudra, Chandrakala Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Release of thumb from Suchi Hasta is Chandrakala Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-09-13 11:45:20', '223.184.62.235', 0, '2024-12-02 02:49:49', '49.37.224.45', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(62, 12, 'Padmakosha', '<p>When all fingers are stretched without touching each other and slightly bent towards the palm, the pose is said to be Padmakosha Mudra. Padmakosha is used to indicate fruits such as wood-apple and bel, bosoms of women, circular movement, ball, cooking vessel, eating, bud, mango, flowers strewn around, bunch of flowers, hibiscus, bell, anthill, lotus and an egg.</p>', '112_19092023111101.jpg', '112_19092023111101.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Padmakosa-Hasta', 'Padmakosha Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras\r\n', 'Padmakosha Hasta Mudra, Padmakosa Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Padmakosha Hasta Mudra is when all fingers are stretched without touching each other and slightly bent towards the palm.', 0, '2023-09-19 11:11:01', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2026-06-02 13:04:58', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(63, 12, 'Sarpashirsa', '<p>When the fingers of Pataka hand are bent at the tip with palm hollowed, it forms the pose called Sarpashirsa Mudra. Sarpashirsa Mudra is used to depict sandal, a serpent, medium tone, libetion of water sprinkling on oneself, nourishment, movement of protrusion of elephant head, combative posture of wrestlers.</p>', '112_19092023113438.jpg', '112_19092023113438.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Sarpasirsa-Hasta', 'Sarpashirsa Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras\r\n', 'Sarpashirsa Hasta Mudra, Sarpashirsa Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Sarpashirsa Mudra is when the fingers of Pataka hand are bent at the tip with palm hollowed.', 0, '2023-09-19 11:34:38', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2024-12-02 03:30:28', '157.46.5.113', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(64, 12, 'Mrigashirsha', '<p>The thumb and little finger of Sarpashirsa are stretched, while rest of the fingers are closely held and bent perpendicular to them, is called Mrigashirsha Mudra. Mrigashirsha Mudra is used to indicate nymphs, cheek, wheel, limitation, anxiety, tussle, attire, calling, the tripartite mark on forehead (religious symbol), a deer, lute, rubbing of feet, coveting others wealth, the female reproductive organ, holding umbrella, stepping and summoning one\'s beloved.</p>', '112_19092023122107.jpg', '112_19092023122107.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Mrgasirsa-Hasta', 'Mrigashirsha Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Mrigashirsha Hasta Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Mrigashirsha Hasta Mudra is when the thump and the little finger of Sarpasirsa are stretched, while rest of the fingers are closely held and bent perpendicular to them.', 0, '2023-09-19 12:21:07', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2026-06-02 13:06:30', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(65, 12, 'Simhamukha', '<p>When all fingers are stretched except the ring and the middle finger, which are pressed against the thumb, it is called Simhamukha Mudra. Simhamukha Mudra is used to represent a fire sacrifice, rabbit, elephant, movement of darbha grass, garland of lotus, face of lion, medicinal preparation of physicians and refinement.</p>', '112_20092023070747.jpg', '112_20092023070747.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Simhamukha-Hasta', 'Simhamukha  Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Simhamukha Hasta Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Simhamukha Hasta Mudra is when all fingers are stretched except the ring and the middle finger, which are pressed against the thumb.', 0, '2023-09-20 07:07:47', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2024-12-02 03:35:03', '157.46.5.113', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(66, 12, 'Kangula', '<p>Ring finger of Padmakosa pose is bend, middle, forefinger and thumb held upwards. Ring finger bend down and little finger raised, is Kangula Mudra. Kangula Mudra is the right pose to represent Lakuca (citrus) fruit, bell-girdle of children, bell, Cakora bird, betel-nut tree, the bosoms of young maiden, white lily flower, coconut and Caataka bird.</p>', '112_20092023072105.jpg', '112_20092023072105.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Kangula-Hasta', 'Kangula Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Kangula Hasta Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Ring finger of Padmakosa pose is bend, middle, forefinger and thumb held upwards. Ring finger bend down and little finger raised is called Kangula Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-09-20 07:21:05', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2024-12-02 03:37:07', '157.46.5.113', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(67, 12, 'Alapadma', '<p>Little finger bend above and all other fingers stretched apart from each other is Alapadma Mudra. In the scriptures, Alapadma Mudra is prescribed to denote moving bloomed lotus, fruits such as wood-apple, circular motion, bosoms, separation from dear one, mirror, full-moon, sense of charm, hair-braid, moon-house, village, altitude, irritancy, a water reservoir, wheel, Cakravaka bird, chirping of birds and eulogy.</p>', '112_20092023091055.jpg', '112_20092023091055.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Alapadma-Hasta', 'Alapadma Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Alapadma Hasta Mudra, Alapadma Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Little finger bend above and all other fingers stretched apart from each other.', 0, '2023-09-20 09:10:55', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2024-12-02 03:54:36', '157.46.5.113', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(68, 12, 'Chatura', '<p>Chatura Mudra is when little finger is straightened and thump is placed at the base of the ring finger with both the middle finger and index finger joined together. Chatura Mudra indicates musk, lesser quantity, gold, copper, iron, dampness, grief, aesthetic pleasure, eyes, castle based difference, substantiative evidence, enjoyment, slower gait, breaking down, face, ghee, oil etc.</p>', '112_20092023115240.jpg', '112_20092023115240.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Catura-Hasta', 'Chatura Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Chatura Hasta Mudra, Catura Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Chatura Hasta Mudra is when little finger is straightened and thump is placed at the base of the ring finger with both the middle finger and index finger joined together', 0, '2023-09-20 11:50:03', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2026-06-02 13:07:53', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(69, 12, 'Bhramara', '<p>When the middle finger and thumb touch each other, index finger bent towards the palm and other two fingers stretched upwards it is called Bhramara Mudra. Bhramara Mudra is used to denote a bee, parrot, wing, heron, cuckoo and other birds.</p>', '112_20092023120544.jpg', '112_20092023120544.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Bhramara-Hasta', 'Bhramara Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Bhramara Hasta Mudra, Bhramara Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'When middle finger and thumb touching each other, index finger bent towards the palm and other two fingers stretched upwards it is Bhramara Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-09-20 12:05:44', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2024-12-02 03:59:40', '157.46.5.113', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(70, 12, 'Hamsasya', '<p>Hamsasya Mudra is when, index finger and thumb pressed against each other and other 3 fingers kept straight upwards, each of the fingers away from one another. Auspicious occasion, tying thread, confirming the imparted knowledge, horripilation, pearl, etc., lighting the wick of lamp, touchstone (stone meant for testing gold), flowers such as jasmine, etc., picture or drawing a picture, a clip and obstructing the flow of water are indicated by Hamsasya Mudra.</p>', '112_20092023121839.jpg', '112_20092023121839.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Hamsasya-Hasta', 'Hamsasya Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Hamsasya Hasta Mudra, Hamsasya Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'When index finger and thumb pressed against each other and other 3 fingers kept straight upwards, each of the fingers away from one another, it is Hamsasya Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-09-20 12:18:39', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2024-12-02 04:00:54', '157.46.5.113', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(71, 12, 'Hamsapaksha', '<p>Hamsapaksha Mudra is when, the ring finger, middle finger and index finger stretched perpendicular to the little finger stretched upwards and thump is bent a little as if to reach to the top of index finger. Hamsapaksha <b></b>Mudra<b></b> is used to depict the numeral six, building of a bridge, engraving with nails and covering.</p>', '112_21092023072453.jpg', '112_21092023072453.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Hamsapksa-Hasta', 'Hamsapaksha Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Hamsapaksha Hasta Mudra, Hamsapaksha Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Hamsapaksha Hasta Mudra is when ring finger, middle finger and index finger stretched perpendicular to the little finger stretched upwards and thump is bent a little as if to reach to the top of index finger.', 0, '2023-09-21 07:24:53', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2026-06-02 13:09:46', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(72, 12, 'Samdamsha', '<p>When the Padmakosa posture fingers are contracted (closed position) and then open-up partly in a repeated manner, the pose is defined as Samdamsha by experts in natya. Samdamsha Mudra it represents numeral five, stomach, offering to deities, injury, an insect, great anxiety, breath and worship according to texts of natya.</p>', '112_21092023091109.jpg', '112_21092023091109.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Sandamsa-Hasta', 'Samdamsha Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Samdamsha Hasta Mudra, Sandamsa Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Samdamsha Hasta Mudra is when the Padmakosa  posture fingers are contracted (closed position) and then open-up partly in a repeated manner.', 0, '2023-09-21 09:11:09', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2026-06-03 04:59:02', '49.37.227.237', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(73, 12, 'Mukula', '<p>Mukula Mudra is defined in scriptures of natya as presentation of all the five fingers together (at the tip). Mukula Mudra is used to depict lilly, eating, Manmatha with his arrows, holding the signet, navel and flower of plantain.</p>', '112_21092023093108.jpg', '112_21092023093108.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Mukula-Hasta', 'Mukula Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Mukula Hasta Mudra, Mukula Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'Mukula Hasta Mudra is defines as presentation of all five fingers together (at the tip).', 0, '2023-09-21 09:31:08', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2024-12-02 04:05:08', '157.46.5.113', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(74, 12, 'Tamrachuda', '<p>When the index finger of Mukula is slightly bent, it is called Tamrachuda Mudra. Tamracuda Mudra is prescribed by knowers of natya to depict rooster etc., heron, crow, camel, calf and engraving.</p>', '112_21092023095945.jpg', '112_21092023095945.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Tamracuda-Hasta', 'Tamrachuda Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Tamrachuda Hasta Mudra, Tamracuda Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'When the index finger of Mukula is slightly bent, it is called Tamrachuda Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-09-21 09:59:45', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2026-06-02 13:10:51', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(75, 12, 'Trishula', '<p>When the thumb and little finger are bent while rest of the fingers are straightened, it is defined as Trishula Mudra. Trishula Mudra gives a sense of holy trinity, bilva leaves and trident.</p>', '112_21092023114356.jpg', '112_21092023114356.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Trisula-Hasta', 'Trishula Hasta Mudra | Single-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras', 'Trishula Hasta Mudra, Trisula Mudra, Asamyuta Hasta, Single-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 28 one hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, non-combined hand gestures', 'When the thumb and the little finger are bent while rest of the fingers are straightened, it is defined as Trishula Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-09-21 11:43:56', '223.190.214.151', 0, '2026-06-02 13:12:09', '49.37.224.53', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(76, 13, 'Samyuta Hasta', '', '113_07112023043447.jpg', '113_07112023043447.jpg', 0, 'y', '', '', '', '', 0, '2023-10-04 09:15:17', '223.184.40.20', 0, '2023-11-07 04:34:47', '116.68.78.173', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(77, 13, 'Anjali', '<p>Anjali Mudra is the joining of two Pataka poses.  Anjali is prescribed by the wise to imply salutations to deities, elders/teachers and twice-born. The hand ought to be placed above the head, in front of the face and in front of the chest (respectively for the three people referred)</p>', '113_10112023112221.jpg', '113_10112023112221.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Anjali-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Anjali Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Classical Dance Mudras | Bharatanatyam | Gallery', 'Anjali Hasta Mudra, Anjali Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta Hasta Picture Gallery', 'Anjali Hasta Mudra is the joining of two Pataka poses.', 0, '2023-10-04 09:34:12', '223.184.40.20', 0, '2024-12-01 17:26:01', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(78, 13, 'Kapota', '<p>Kapota Mudra is the pose wherein the two Pataka hands are joined and cupped towards the finger tips, sides and base of the pose. Kapota is applied to depict respectful salutation, conversation with teachers, mark of obedience and acceptance.</p>', '113_10112023112258.jpg', '113_10112023112258.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Kapota-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Kapota Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras | Gallery', 'Kapota Hasta Mudra, Kapota Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures,  Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Kapota Mudra is the pose in which the two Pataka hands are joined and cupped towards the finger tips, sides and base of the palms.', 0, '2023-10-04 10:35:40', '223.184.40.20', 0, '2024-12-01 17:10:27', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(79, 13, 'Karkata', '<p>Karkata Mudra is the pose where the fingers of both hands are interlocked and stretched across. Karkata Mudra is applied to indicate arrival of many (people), sight of belly, blowing the conch, stretching the limbs and bending a bench.</p>', '113_10112023112350.jpg', '113_10112023112350.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Karkata-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Karkata Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Karkata Hasta Mudra, Karkata Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Karkata Hasta Mudra is the pose where the fingers of both hands are interlocked and stretched across.', 0, '2023-10-04 10:53:02', '223.184.40.20', 0, '2024-12-01 17:13:34', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(80, 13, 'Svastika', '<p>Svastika Mudra pose is formed when the two Pataka pose are held across and held together at the wrist. Svastika is used to denote a crocodile.</p>', '113_10112023112429.jpg', '113_10112023112429.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Svastika-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Svastika Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras | Gallery', 'Svastika Hasta Mudra, Svastika Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Svastika Hasta Mudra pose is formed when the two Pataka pose are held across and held together at the wrist.', 0, '2023-10-04 12:02:52', '223.184.40.20', 0, '2024-12-01 17:14:58', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(81, 13, 'Dola', '<p>\r\n\r\nDola Mudra is formed when the Pataka pose is placed along the sides of the thighs. At the commencement of natya, Dola is the pose prescribed by experts.</p>', '113_10112023112456.jpg', '113_10112023112456.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Dola-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Dola Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudras | Gallery', 'Dola Hasta Mudra, Dola Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Dola Hasta Mudra is formed when the Pataka pose is placed along the sides of the thighs.', 0, '2023-10-16 12:25:59', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 17:17:23', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(82, 13, 'Puspaputa', '<p>Puspaputa Mudra is formed when two Sarpasirsa are held together. Puspaputa is utilized for indicating waving of lights, acceptance of water, fruits, etc., offering to Gods, dusk and tributes paid with incantations (i.e., mantras act like floral tributes).</p>', '113_10112023112525.jpg', '113_10112023112525.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Puspaputa-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Puspaputa Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Puspaputa Hasta Mudra, Puspaputa Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Puspaputa Hasta Mudra is formed when two Sarpasirsa are held together.', 0, '2023-10-17 08:33:37', '116.68.77.173', 0, '2024-12-01 17:18:40', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(83, 13, 'Utsanga', '<p>Utsanga Mudra is formed according to the masters of natya when two Mrigasirsa poses are placed on the upper arms of the opposite sides.  Utsanga is used to indicate tight embrace, bashfulness, display of armlets, etc., and training the boys.</p>', '113_10112023112556.jpg', '113_10112023112556.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Utsanga-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Utsanga Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Utsanga Hasta Mudra, Utsanga Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Utsanga Hasta Mudra is formed when two Mrigasirsa poses are placed on the upper arms of the opposite sides.', 0, '2023-10-17 08:42:34', '116.68.77.173', 0, '2024-12-01 17:19:34', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(84, 13, 'Sivalinga', '<p>When Sikhara pose of right hand is placed over the Ardhachandra pose of left hand, the resultant is called Sivalinga Mudra. Sivalinga pose is to indicate the linga (representation) of Siva.</p>', '113_10112023112625.jpg', '113_10112023112625.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Sivalinga-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Sivalinga Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'SIvalinga Hasta Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'When Sikhara pose of right hand is placed over the Ardhacandra pose of left hand, the resultant is called Sivalinga Mudra.', 0, '2023-10-17 16:36:07', '116.68.77.173', 0, '2024-12-01 17:21:07', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(85, 13, 'Katakavardhana', '<p>When the two Katakamukha poses are crossed at the wrist, forming a Svastika, the pose is called as Katakavardhana Mudra according to dancers. Katakavardhana Mudra is used to indicate coronation ceremony, worship and nuptial bond.</p>', '113_10112023112700.jpg', '113_10112023112700.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Katakavardhana-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Katakavardhana Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Katakavardhana Hasta Mudra, Katakavardhana Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Katakavardhana Hasta Mudra is when the two Katakamukha poses are crossed at the wrist, forming a Svastika.', 0, '2023-10-18 05:20:15', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 17:22:40', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(86, 13, 'Kartarisvastika', '<p>Both hands showing Kartarimukha poses held at wrists form a Svastika. This pose is called as Kartarisvastika. Kartarisvastika Mudra denotes branches, peaks of hills and trees.</p>', '113_18102023060723.jpg', '113_18102023060723.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Kartarisvastika-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Kartarisvastika Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Kartarisvastika Hasta Mudra, Kartarisvastika Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Both hands showing Kartarimukha poses held at wrists form a Svastika. This pose is called as Kartarisvastika Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-10-18 06:07:23', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 17:23:56', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(87, 13, 'Sakata', '<p>When both the middle fingers and the thumb are separated in Bhramara pose the gesture is called Sakata Mudra. Sakata pose is used to denote a demon and found to be used in playing his role.</p>', '113_10112023113456.jpg', '113_10112023113456.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Sakata-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Sakata Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Sakata Hasta Mudra, sakata mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'When both the middle fingers and the thumb are separated in Bhramara pose the gesture is called Sakata Mudra.', 0, '2023-10-18 08:22:51', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 17:08:49', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(88, 13, 'Sankha', '<p>When the thumb of one hand meets the thumb of the Sikhara of the other hand, with its fore-finger clasping the thumb, the pose is called Sankha Mudra. Sankha Mudra denotes conch etc., things in its shape according to Bharata and others.</p>', '113_10112023113552.jpg', '113_10112023113552.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Sankha-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Sankha Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Sankha Hasta Mudra, Sankha Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Sankha Hasta Mudra is formed when the thumb of one hand meets the thumb of the Sikhara of the other hand, with its fore-finger clasping  the thumb.', 0, '2023-10-18 08:45:01', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 17:07:33', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(89, 13, 'Chakra', '<p>Chakra Mudra is resultant when the palms of the Ardhacandra touch each other with one hand vertical and the other placed horizontally over the other. Chakra Mudra indicates a wheel.</p>', '113_10112023113627.jpg', '113_10112023113627.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Cakra-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Chakra Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Cakra Hasta Mudra, Chakra Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Cakra Hasta Mudra is resultant when the palms of the Ardhacandra touch each other with one hand vertical and the other placed horizontally over the other.', 0, '2023-10-18 08:53:39', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 17:05:49', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(90, 13, 'Pasa', '<p>When the index fingers of Suci are bent inwardly and joined, the gesture is called Pasa Mudra. Pasa <b></b>Mudra<b></b> is used to indicate mutual tussle, chain and noose. </p>', '113_10112023113703.jpg', '113_10112023113703.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Pasa-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Pasa Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Pasa Hasta Mudra, Pasa Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'When the index fingers of Suci are bent inwardly and joined, gesture is called Pasa Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-10-18 10:15:50', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 17:02:12', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(91, 13, 'Kilaka', '<p>When in Mrigasirsa, the little fingers are inwardly bent and joined, they form Kilaka Mudra. Kilaka Mudra is used to indicate love and jocular conversation.</p>', '113_10112023113742.jpg', '113_10112023113742.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Kilaka-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Kilaka Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Kilaka Hasta Mudra, Kilaka Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'When in Mrigasirsa, the little fingers are inwardly bent and joined, they form Kilaka Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-10-18 10:31:42', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 16:57:14', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(92, 13, 'Matsya', '<p>When the thumbs and little finger are out-stretched and one hand\'s palm is placed on the back of the other palm it forms the Matsya Mudra. Matsya Mudra is used to indicate a fish.</p>', '113_10112023113814.jpg', '113_10112023113814.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Matsya-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Matsya Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Matsya Hasta Mudra, Matsya Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Matsya Hasta Mudra is when the thumbs and little finger are out-stretched and one hand\'s palm is placed on the back of the other palm.', 0, '2023-10-18 10:41:51', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 16:55:25', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(93, 13, 'Kurma', '<p>Kurma Mudra is formed when the tip of thumb and little fingers in Chakra are stretched and remaining fingers are intertwined. Kurma Mudra is to depict a tortoise.</p>', '113_10112023113845.jpg', '113_10112023113845.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Kurma-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Kurma Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Kurma Hasta Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Kurma Hasta Mudra is formed when the tip of thumb and little fingers in Chakra are stretched and remaining fingers are intertwined.', 0, '2023-10-18 11:02:04', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 16:53:28', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(94, 13, 'Varaha', '<p>\r\n\r\nVaraha Mudra is formed when the two Mrigasirsa hands are placed one upon the other with one hand\'s thumb joining the other hand\'s little finger and others outstretched. Varaha Mudra is to depict a boar.</p>', '113_10112023113920.jpg', '113_10112023113920.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Varaha-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Varaha Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Varaha Hasta Mudra, varaha mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Varaha Hasta Mudra is when two Mrigasirsa hands are placed one upon the other with one hand\'s thumb joining the other hand\'s little finger and others outstretched.', 0, '2023-10-18 12:07:10', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 16:50:29', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(95, 13, 'Garuda', '<p>\r\n\r\nGaruda Mudra is when the thumbs of two Ardhacandra are placed on each other with hand stretched out on either directions and with thumbs interlocked. Garuda Mudra is to indicate a hawk (Garuda).</p>', '113_10112023113945.jpg', '113_10112023113945.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Garuda-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Garuda Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Garuda Hasta Mudra, Garuda Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Garuda Hasta Mudra is when the thumbs of two Ardhacandra are placed on each other with hand stretched out on either directions and with thumbs interlocked.', 0, '2023-10-18 12:14:33', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 16:48:38', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(96, 13, 'Nagabandha', '<p>\r\n\r\nThe Sarpasirsa crossed with Svastika hands forms Nagabandha Mudra. Nagabandha Mudra is to denote the twining of snake.</p>', '113_10112023114101.jpg', '113_10112023114101.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Nagabandha-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Nagabandha Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Nagabandha Hasta Mudra, Nagabandha Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'The Sarpasirsa crossed with Svastika hands forms Nagabandha Hasta Mudra.', 0, '2023-10-18 12:20:19', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 16:47:30', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(97, 13, 'Katva', '<p>\r\n\r\nKatva Mudra is formed when one Catura hand is placed over another Catura hand with the index finger and thumb of both the hands stretched out.  Katva Mudra is used to indicate a cot and palanquin.</p>', '113_10112023114131.jpg', '113_10112023114131.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Katva-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Katva Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Katva Hasta Mudra,  Katva Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Katva Hasta Mudra is formed when one Catura hand is placed over another Catura hand with the index finger and thumb of both the hands stretched out.', 0, '2023-10-20 05:07:51', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 16:46:11', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
(98, 13, 'Bherunda', '<p>\r\n\r\nBherunda Mudra is formed when two Kapittha hands are held together at wrists.  Bherunda Mudra indicates Bherunda (an mythological figure) and a bird-pair.</p>', '113_10112023114205.jpg', '113_10112023114205.jpg', 0, 'n', 'Bherunda-Hasta-Bharatanatyam', 'Bherunda Hasta Mudra | Combined-Hand Gesture | Bharatanatyam | Mudra | Gallery', 'Bherunda Hasta Mudra, Samyuta Hasta, Combined-Hand Gesture, Abhinayadarpanam, 23 Combined hand gestures in Bharatanatyam, Mudras in Classical Dance, Hasta Bhedah, Hand Postures, Combined hand gestures, Samyuta hasta picture gallery', 'Bherunda Hasta Mudra is formed when two Kapittha hands are held together at wrists.', 0, '2023-10-20 05:17:56', '171.49.173.198', 0, '2024-12-01 16:44:55', '49.37.227.212', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1);
