oved></div> <div xss=removed></div></div></a><p xss=removed><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DQgT3JwDtVr/?utm_source=ig_embed&utm_campaign=loading\" target=\"_blank\">A post shared by NatyaSutra (@natyasutraonline)</a></p></div></blockquote>', 'In this Odissi Beginner’s Class, Vidushi Sujatha Mohapatra introduces the Asamyuta Hasta Mudras, which are single-hand gestures that form the foundation of expressive dance in Odissi. This lesson focuses on the 28 Asamyuta Hastas, each representing a unique movement, idea, or emotion used in storytelling and performance. Ideal for beginners, this session in Natyasutra online provides a clear understanding of how each gesture contributes to the grammar of Odissi dance and lays the groundwork for further exploration of abhinaya and technique.                           ', '1-28112025081532.jpg', NULL, 7, 'asamyuta-hasta-mudras', 'Odissi Beginner’s Class | Asamyuta Hasta Mudras with Vidushi Sujata Mohapatra | NatyaSutraOnline', 'Odissi dance, Odissi beginners, Asamyuta Hasta Mudras, Odissi hand gestures, Odissi tutorial, Sujata Mohapatra, Odissi abhinaya, classical Indian dance, Odissi online class, NatyaSutraOnline', 'In this Odissi beginner’s tutorial, Vidushi Sujata Mohapatra introduces the Asamyuta Hasta Mudras, or single-hand gestures, which form the foundation of Odissi classical dance. This lesson covers all 28 Asamyuta Hastas, each symbolizing distinct movements, emotions, and expressions essential to storytelling and abhinaya.', 0, '2025-11-05 06:39:11', '49.37.234.72', 0, '2026-09-10 11:11:39', '49.37.226.45', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1);
