(104, 8, 0, 'Ganapati Maam... Thiruvathirakali', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ba_3PUwKcCg', 'Embodying grace and charm, Thiruvathirakali involves a group of women dance around a Nilavilakku (Traditional wick lamp) in a circular motion. Also known as Kaikottikali, the performance is accompanied by clapping and singing.  Traditionally it was performed in Kerala as part of the major festivals such as Onam.         ', '1-28112025081438.jpg', NULL, 4, 'ganapati-maam-thiruvathirakali', 'Ganapati Maam | Thiruvathira Dance, Traditional Art Form of Kerala', 'thiruvathirakkali, thiruvathira, ganapathi maam, Thiruvathirakali, Kaikottikali, Kerala traditional dance, Nilavilakku, women’s group dance, Onam festival dance, Kerala folk arts, Thiruvathira, Kerala culture, Kaikotti kali, Kerala heritage arts, festival folk dance', 'Embodying grace and tradition, Thiruvathirakali, also known as Kaikottikali, is a Kerala group dance performed by women around a Nilavilakku, featuring rhythmic clapping, singing, and circular movements, especially during festivals like Onam.', 0, '2025-11-19 03:56:03', '49.37.232.170', 0, '2025-11-28 08:14:38', '49.37.233.141', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
