=removed></div></div></a><p xss=removed><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DQgT3JwDtVr/?utm_source=ig_embed&utm_campaign=loading\" target=\"_blank\">A post shared by NatyaSutra (@natyasutraonline)</a></p></div></blockquote>', 'What can a single mudra convey?\r\n\r\nA thought. A feeling. A moment. Sometimes. Even a whole world.\r\n\r\nIn Odissi, the 28 Asamyuta Hasta Mudras are the building blocks of its expressive tradition — each gesture with its own movement, meaning and purpose.\r\n\r\nIn this beginner’s class, Vidushi Sujata Mohapatra takes you through these beautiful single-hand gestures, opening up the expressive world of Odissi and showing how much can unfold through the movement of a hand.\r\n\r\nAnd as we celebrate 3 million views on Natyasutra Online, what better way to celebrate than with the gestures that give Odissi so much of its expressive power?\r\n\r\nOne mudra. A world of expression.', '1-10092026110321.jpg', NULL, 2, 'asamyuta-hastas-3-million', 'Asamyuta Hasta Mudras with Vidushi Sujata Mohapatra | Odissi Beginner’s Class | NatyaSutraOnline', 'Odissi dance, Odissi beginners, Asamyuta Hasta Mudras, Odissi hand gestures, Odissi tutorial, Sujata Mohapatra, Odissi abhinaya, classical Indian dance, Odissi online class, NatyaSutraOnline', 'In this Odissi beginner’s tutorial, Vidushi Sujata Mohapatra introduces the Asamyuta Hasta Mudras, or single-hand gestures, which form the foundation of Odissi classical dance. This lesson covers all 28 Asamyuta Hastas, each symbolizing distinct movements, emotions, and expressions essential to storytelling and abhinaya.', 0, '2026-09-10 11:01:38', '49.37.226.45', 0, '2026-09-10 11:32:32', '49.37.226.45', 0, '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 1),
